summary:
  The unsteady line names one member again: the first that answered.

history:
  The check cannot tell which speaker would not hold still. It reads the
  difference between them, and that is what would not settle. The name on
  the line was whichever member came first in the list and had been heard
  at all. On 2026-11-11 that put "DRIFT_UNSTEADY bluez_output..." into the
  journal forty-one times, and it read as the Bluetooth speaker being at
  fault, which nothing had shown. A room on paper where the wired member
  is the one that answers late prints the Bluetooth one's name just the
  same.

target:
  package/contents/ui/calibrate.py

find:
                        % " ".join(members[k][0] for k in sorted(heard_ever)))

replace:
                        % members[min(heard_ever)][0])

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_calibrate.py::test_an_unsteady_room_names_every_member_that_answered_not_the_first.
  Line-neutral.
